From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vladimir Skvortsov <vskvortsov@emcraft.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 11:22:55 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] wlconf: return 0 when the output file is written

write_file() returns ret uninitialised on success, so the exit status of
a run that wrote a correct file is whatever was on the stack.

Upstream-Status: Inactive-Upstream [lastcommit: 2017, lastrelease: R8.8]
Signed-off-by: Vladimir Skvortsov <vskvortsov@emcraft.com>
---
 wlconf/main.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/wlconf/main.c b/wlconf/main.c
index 6a4d8ae..f0c9d20 100644
--- a/wlconf/main.c
+++ b/wlconf/main.c
@@ -557,7 +557,7 @@ static void free_file(void *buffer)
 static int write_file(const char *filename, const void *buffer, size_t size)
 {
 	FILE *file;
-	int ret;
+	int ret = 0;
 
 	file = fopen(filename, "w");
 	if (!file) {
